argument_evidence.context_text:
[18] CARL challenges the legality of the four JGs on the following grounds:
Paragraph 159(1)(h) does not authorize the Chairperson to issue a JG with respect to issues of fact;
The JGs unlawfully fetter Board members’ discretion and improperly encroach upon their adjudicative independence;
The JGs unfairly enhance the burden of proof on claimants for refugee protection; and
The JGs were issued without any external consultation.

